            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The product is the cube of the middle term; use the sum to find the common ratio.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Let the terms be $\\frac{b}{r},b,br$, where $r\\ne0$. Their product gives\n$$\\begin{align*}b^3&=-8\\\\b&=-2.\\end{align*}$$\nUsing their sum,\n$$\\begin{align*}-\\frac{2}{r}-2-2r&=\\frac{14}{3}\\\\3r^2+10r+3&=0\\\\(3r+1)(r+3)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nThus $r=-\\frac13$ or $r=-3$, giving $6,-2,\\frac23$ or $\\frac23,-2,6$.\n\nCheck: $6-2+\\frac23=\\frac{14}{3}$ and $6(-2)\\frac23=-8$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 85
